id: pm-review-conflicting-verdicts
title: Expose conflicting verdict witnesses without voting them away
description: "AC1: Opposed explicit fix and refuse judgments on one confirmed finding lineage and exact artifact scope yield both source identities in a bounded read-only decision packet. AC2: Provider counts and decision recency never settle conflict. AC3: Withdrawn or unavailable reviews cannot settle conflict. AC4: Typed SDK and CLI share strict validation, compact JSON/TOON, typed remedies, docs, model-based and no-git evidence, public tracker measurements and passing CI npm/Bun release gates. Overlap rechecked against pinned core SDK declarations and sibling pm-web: findingLineage/lineageGroups supply confirmed finding identity; core PmClient.planDecision and native Plan decisions remain authoritative; pm-web decision inbox owns human request/response. This feature only projects review-specific incompatible judgments and missing resolution evidence; it adds no persistence, vote aggregation, import, sync, journal or resolution workflow."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-28T21:20:48.734Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T22:11:03.255Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Two opposed explicit judgments at one confirmed lineage and exact artifact scope yield both original source identities; Provider counts and recency never resolve votes; Withdrawn or unavailable reviews cannot settle the conflict; Typed SDK and CLI return bounded JSON/TOON packets and typed remedies; Seeded 500-sequence SDK read-back, native fields, relationships, replay, custom-status, no-git, interleaving, public-data and packed-install evidence pass; CI npm and Bun release gates pass at unchanged thresholds"
parent: pm-review-epic
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T21:22:55.675Z",codex-agent,"Design: reuse lineageGroups, complete native SDK reads, requestSnapshot verified history addressing and scopeDigest; command uses host-injected PmClient. Exact scope is GitHub repo/PR/revision or envelope origin/subject/revision. Only explicit fix versus refuse are opposed; pending, stale, duplicate and informational do not imply rejection. Read-only packets preserve all raw current judgments, including withdrawn sources, and mark missing core decision, resolution evidence and availability. No tracker mutations, leases, journal, import/export/sync or ambient create defaults are added. Tests will exercise SDK read-back, seeded 500-sequence replay/relationship changes, custom statuses, extreme metadata, every read boundary, packed installers and public non-git input fingerprints."
  "2026-10-28T21:36:40.686Z",codex-agent,"Public read-only export validation at origin/main 06cd671: 63 items, 22 ReviewFindings and 22 lineage/scopes; 17 packets with 15 explicit judgments and 2 non-explicit skips; 5 typed input_invalid refusals for historical observations without a source revision. No natural opposition in this public corpus. Maximum JSON 1518 bytes, TOON 1411 bytes; 17 CRLF query replays matched; all 132 native input files unchanged. Sources were exported outside git with native files read-only. Synthetic opposing-source regressions supply positive acceptance evidence. Typecheck, lint, docstring and zero-duplication gates passed; randomized, interleaving and packed-global checks continue."
  "2026-10-28T21:43:07.584Z",codex-agent,"Concurrency evidence: the focused interleaving regression passed all 31 SDK step boundaries for seven real peer transitions (217 cases) on one plain non-git tracker: verdict, exact A-B-A restoration, source scope, lineage, retyping, anchor scope and anchor retyping. Every peer transition is preserved. Custom status roles and random ambient focus also passed; no writer, lease, claim, outbox or journal is added. Linked pm test ran npm run typecheck && npm run lint and passed (1/1)."
  "2026-10-28T21:52:53.590Z",codex-agent,"Local model passed: seed 3237023784, 500 random sequences, 995 operations, 96 native fields, 157 older-value replays and 34 conflict cases; SDK read-back, relationships and native histories unchanged; JSON/TOON and CRLF transport round trips matched. Boundary regressions passed 6/6; npm global and Bun global packed acceptance passed 1/1. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy changed only reviewConflicts to omit opposition: named opposed-judgments regression failed with no_opposition_observed versus conflict; fixed worktree subsequently passed. Final public measurement after remedy text stabilization: maximum JSON 1554 bytes, TOON 1447; all other counts remain 63 items, 22 scopes, 17 packets, 15 judgments, 2 skips, 5 missing-revision refusals, 17 CRLF replays and 132 unchanged native inputs. Isolated health passed; ambient health has a global extension host-version skew. CI is the full-gate authority."
  "2026-10-28T21:54:56.684Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/pull/61. Implementation commit 8fc73b6 contains code, docs, model/interleaving tests and append-only tracker evidence. Planned tracker writes finish with this handoff; exact final-head npm/Bun release-gate run URLs and counts are reported on the PR and its checks at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/pull/61/checks. CI release gates use unchanged thresholds. This package only emits observed conflict evidence and never grants approval or persists a resolution. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification and closure; releasing only the codex-agent claim."
  "2026-10-28T22:08:57.376Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI run 40775900349 found one integration fixture mismatch: extension activation still expected 16 commands, while the new conflicts command correctly registers the seventeenth. Node 26 completed 306 tests with 305 pass and that one failure; all executable conflict code measured 100 percent in every coverage dimension. The new erased type-contract module also needs the same explicit runtime loading used by existing pure-type modules so full-source coverage accounts for it. Updating the command registry contract assertion and loading the type-contract module, without changing thresholds or runtime feature behavior; then targeted checks and fresh exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-28T22:11:01.480Z",codex-agent,"CI fixture repair verified locally: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='extension activation exposes|compact JSON/TOON' test/core.test.ts test/conflicts.test.ts passed 2/2. Explicitly loading the pure type module matched existing package practice and the targeted full-source type-module coverage check passed 100/100/100/100 (1 test). Test typecheck, lint and zero duplication passed. Runtime feature code is unchanged; thresholds are unchanged. Releasing the codex-agent claim and pushing these complete tracker writes before fresh exact-head CI. Final run receipts remain on PR 61."
